# Joint route optimization: capability pilot

Frozen after the free reference and mutation gates, before any route model call.
This authored task is separate from inventory reconciliation. It is a candidate
for greater difficulty, not an established hard benchmark or novel result.

## Task and sample

Find two distinct directed source-to-sink paths minimizing their combined cost,
with no shared internal node or internal risk group. Repeated risk within one
route is allowed. Endpoints are exempt from disjointness. All edge costs are
positive integers; graphs are acyclic, contain at most ten nodes and at most 64
source-to-sink paths. Return -1 exactly when no admissible pair exists.

The auditor receives the full contract/schema, query parameters, claimed optimum,
publisher SQL, truthful execution receipt, and truthful database integrity check.
It can query the read-only graph and submits a verdict, probability the claim is
true, and executable SQL computing the optimum. Final program grading is not fed
back. Use Luna/medium Responses, strict schemas, at most eight responses/eight
queries, 4096 output tokens, unchanged isolation and conservative accounting.
The model is told its program will be tested on other contract-conforming graphs.

Eight no-peer episodes: seeds 14001–14004, each with a correct and flawed publisher
program. Within a seed, graph data are identical. The correct program optimizes
over all compatible pairs. The flawed program first picks a cheapest path and
only then optimizes its partner. Ties use an explicit textual route ordering.
The claimed cost always equals the actual publisher program's output. Graphs are
qualified using references alone so that this shortcut produces a wrong claim.
Record qualification candidate index; do not select using model outcomes or
interpret this enriched sample as prevalence in deployment. Fixed shuffled order.

## Validity and replay

Python path enumeration and SQL recursion agree on all 1,024 five-node DAGs under
three risk assignments. The live gate passed eight planned cases and 30 replay
conditions within the actual query limits. Nine authored wrong queries have
counterexamples. The first replay gate missed the greedy error; its outcome-blind
amendment before model inference is documented in route-development.md.

Replay each submitted program unchanged on seeds 15001–15008: one reference-
qualified greedy trap, one ordinary graph, and a renamed copy of the ordinary
graph with different endpoints for each seed, plus six fixed boundary graphs.
Thirty conditions per program are not independent model replications. Report
success by condition type and all-world success; never repair an agent's program.
Inspect all live queries and justifications. Source/parameter reasoning is valid
evidence; query count alone does not establish adequate verification.

The fixed cost claims concern finite observed graphs; fresh program correctness
is a separate endpoint. A correct verdict can accompany a poorly generalizing
program. A failed query is an observation the agent can learn from, subject to
its fixed budget. Invalid model actions end the episode and stop this pilot.

## Decision and spending

The question is whether the auditor can recover the joint optimum and a reusable
verifier in the presence of a plausible inherited shortcut. If capability fails,
diagnose whether semantics, tool limits, or algorithm construction caused it
before any peer comparison. If all programs are correct immediately, record
another ceiling; do not label it hard or scale simply to hunt for failure.
If the task yields nontrivial but interpretable verification behavior, freeze
competing hypotheses and a fresh experiment. No automatic treatment matrix.

Maximum batch reservation $2.2, worst-case $2.179072 for 64 requests. Phase before
dispatch: 406 requests, $0.398673375 charges, $5.695159000 retained reservations;
use the same $25 ledger. Stop on incomplete episodes, reference inconsistencies,
provider/accounting failures, or Daybreak rejection. No retry, fallback, replacement,
or alternate route. Preserve results regardless of direction or usefulness.
